1
00:00:32,783 --> 00:00:37,746
And on that point,
members of the jury, I rest my case.

2
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,810
(Camera clicks)

3
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:04,606
(Alarm)

4
00:01:31,842 --> 00:01:33,927
Hello, Wanda.

5
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:48,919
- Hi, Ken.
- Hello, W-W-Wanda.

6
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:53,256
Ken... this is Otto.

7
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,592
Hello. Wanda's told me a lot about you.

8
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:57,594
Hey! Great fish!

9
00:02:57,761 --> 00:03:00,430
A little squeeze of lemon,
some tartare sauce, perfect!

10
00:03:02,057 --> 00:03:03,850
George back yet?

11
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:07,229
No. He had to g-g-go to the b-b-b...

12
00:03:12,234 --> 00:03:13,819
What?

13
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:17,197
That's quite a stutter
you've got there, Ken.

14
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:21,952
It's all right, it doesn't bother me.
So George needs a weapons man, eh?

15
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:24,538
A cup of tea, Ken?

16
00:03:24,705 --> 00:03:26,289
Y-y-y...

17
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,458
Yeah. He'd like one.

18
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,837
I had a good friend in the CIA
had a stutter. Cost him his life.

19
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:34,131
(Door opens)

20
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:37,426
Hi, George.

21
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:41,513
Hello, George. Get you a Scotch?

22
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,348
Yeah.

23
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:46,935
George... this is Otto.

24
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:51,523
So, you're Wanda's brother.

25
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:55,318
It's good to be here, George.
England is a fine country.

26
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:58,321
She tell you what we need?

27
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:04,369
(Ken gasps)

28
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:09,499
Something like that?

29
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,919
Something like that.

30
00:04:14,838 --> 00:04:16,965
Hello, Wendy.

31
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:20,802
Had a good day?

32
00:04:21,303 --> 00:04:24,055
I spend the morning trying
to get a waste-disposal man,

33
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:27,976
have lunch with Marjorie, who kept
complaining about her husband,

34
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:30,896
then I have to play
three rubbers with Philippa.

35
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:33,940
And now Sanderson's
have sent the wrong flowers.

36
00:04:34,065 --> 00:04:35,692
Oh, no!

37
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:40,864
- Would you like some tea?
- Yes.

38
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:43,742
I won the case.

39
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:46,203
This is my first moment
of peace all day.

40
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:54,836
- Hello, Portia. How was the show?
- Awful. I've got to have a new horse

41
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,964
- I thought you liked Phantom.
- He's not fit for dog meat.

42
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:01,718
- Can I change him? It won't cost much.
- Oughtn't we to ask...

43
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:04,888
I thought you were making tea, Archie.
I'd better do it.

44
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:08,058
- Let me do it.
- No, I'll do it!

45
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:15,273
- I won the case.
- Oh! Now this is cracked.

46
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:20,195
They're worth about 100,000 each.

47
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:24,699
There are 135 of them.
That makes 13 millions, my friends.

48
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:27,702
- Dollars or pounds?
- Pounds, pet.

49
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:30,455
This is the big one. So...

50
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:33,458
OK.

51
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:35,377
Yeah.

52
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:38,046
Otto?

53
00:05:38,213 --> 00:05:40,298
- Yes?
- OK?

54
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:43,301
- What?
- The plan.

55
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:46,263
Yeah. Great. No problem.

56
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,932
What was the middle thing,
about the police?

57
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:52,894
We don't meet up
at Heathrow until Tuesday...

58
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:56,189
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
- I haven't finished yet.

59
00:05:56,314 --> 00:06:00,277
Because the police will watch
all the airports for 72 hours.

60
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:02,362
I know. I know.

61
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:07,951
Do you want m-m-me to g-g-get a b-b-big

62
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:11,621
c-c-car?

63
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,666
Yes, Ken. A limo, OK?

64
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:17,460
And put diplomatic plates on it, right?

65
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:19,588
What if he has to speak
in the break-in?

66
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:22,007
Nobody says anything during
a break-in.

67
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:24,801
It's OK, Otto. Ken's good.

68
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:29,431
So next week we won't
have to look for work.

69
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,934
And it won't have to look for us.

70
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:35,186
Oscar Wilde.

71
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:43,862
You really like animals, don't you, Ken?
What's the attraction?

72
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:49,492
Because you can t-t-trust them,
and they don't sh-sh-sh...

73
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:53,163
- Shit on you?
- Show off all the time.

74
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:58,418
Know what Nietzsche said about them?
He said they were God's second blunder.

75
00:06:58,585 --> 00:07:00,086
Bye, sis.

76
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:04,591
Well, you t-tell him from me
that I-I-I...

77
00:07:04,716 --> 00:07:06,343
Bye, George.

78
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:09,137
If you talk to Mom, tell her I said hi.

79
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:11,306
- OK.
- (Whispers) Don't let him touch you.

80
00:07:11,473 --> 00:07:13,224
One more day, we're together.

81
00:07:16,937 --> 00:07:20,607
I'm sorry about my brother, Ken.
I know he's insensitive.

82
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:25,236
He's had a hard life.
Dad used to beat him up.

83
00:07:29,366 --> 00:07:30,492
Good.

84
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:33,912
- (Man yells)
- (Screaming)

85
00:08:55,869 --> 00:08:59,039
(George) Anybody moves
and you're dead!

86
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,478
(Alarm)

87
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:27,776
(Dogs yap)

88
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:32,822
Look where you're going! Chauvinist pig!

89
00:09:33,490 --> 00:09:37,035
Really! People here just think
they own the pavement!

90
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,789
(Engine starts)

91
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:46,628
(Brakes screech)

92
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:08,233
That was fun. I love robbing the
English. They're so polite.

93
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:10,360
- The d-d-d...
- What is it, Ken?

94
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:13,113
- The dog!
- We didn't hit the dog, Ken. It's OK.

95
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,115
$20 million,
he worried about an insect.

96
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:16,699
It's not an-an-an...

97
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:18,368
Stutter's not getting any better, is it?

98
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:19,786
Shut up!

99
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:22,038
- Shut up!
- (Siren)

100
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:29,921
Ken?

101
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:32,882
Bye.

102
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:05,957
- Let's split.
- Heathrow, Tuesday.

103
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:09,335
- Lie low. No celebrating.
- No celebrating?

104
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:13,006
- See you in a couple of hours.
- OK. Bye.

105
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:03,765
- To 20 million.
- To a job well done.

106
00:12:03,932 --> 00:12:05,058
To us.

107
00:12:05,225 --> 00:12:08,061
To the best
brother-and-sister team since...

108
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:10,230
Romeo and Juliet?

109
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:14,484
Do you believe those cockney klutzes
bought our story? What morons!

110
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:16,694
- I want you to know something.
- What?

111
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:20,490
Even if you were my brother,
I'd still want to fuck you.

112
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,617
Oooh!

113
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:25,912
- Make the call.
- Momento, carissima.

114
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,872
No. No Italian!

115
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:29,040
Hey!

116
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:35,171
Per cominciare, due insalate verdi
con peperoni e un linguini primavera.

117
00:12:35,338 --> 00:12:38,049
No. Make the call, Otto.

118
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:42,553
- Are you really Italian?
- Absolutamente. Si.

119
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:46,349
My name is Otto. It means eight.
Say "Arrivederci a Giorgio."

120
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:49,560
- Bye, George.
- (Italian accent) Police, please.

121
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:51,646
- Otto!
- Argh!

122
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:56,734
(English accent) Hello.
I thought it might interest you to know

123
00:12:56,901 --> 00:13:00,238
that the Hatton Garden robbery
today was pulled off

124
00:13:00,405 --> 00:13:03,992
by a Mr. George Thomason, who lives at

125
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:06,828
Flat 3, Kipling Mansions,

126
00:13:06,995 --> 00:13:10,581
Murray Road, London, West 9.

127
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,667
Wanda?

128
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:25,513
(Siren)

129
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:37,775
Police! Open up!

130
00:13:39,694 --> 00:13:41,904
Come on, open up!

131
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:47,410
Open the door, or we'll knock it down.

132
00:13:57,754 --> 00:13:59,672
George Francis Thomason?

133
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:14,979
Passport, tickets...

134
00:14:15,146 --> 00:14:17,065
...money.

135
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:23,654
- (Horn)
- (Otto) Asshole!

136
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:25,490
(Crash)

137
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:36,334
- We're rich, Wanda.
- Yep?

138
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,337
I bet these last two weeks with me

139
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:42,215
have been the most exciting
two weeks of your life.

140
00:14:42,382 --> 00:14:44,342
You said it.

141
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,770
(Breathes deeply)

142
00:14:55,937 --> 00:14:57,438
OK.

143
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,649
OK.

144
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:01,484
Disappointed!

145
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,278
Son of a bitch!

146
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:07,490
What do you have to do in this life
to make people trust you?

147
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,117
Shut up.

148
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:11,661
People always take advantage of me.

149
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:13,830
Shut up and think.
Where's he moved it?

150
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:20,378
- What are you doing?
- I'm thinking!

151
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:22,255
Thinking what I'll do to him.

152
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:24,340
First, I'll hang him up
with piano wire...

153
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:27,135
- Where are you going?
- To talk to him.

154
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:29,011
Then...

155
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:31,180
Talk to who? Talk to who?!

156
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:34,559
So while installing windows
for your parents,

157
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:38,354
you were kneeling on the floor
where there was broken glass?

158
00:15:38,521 --> 00:15:41,649
- That's right, sir.
- And your parents can confirm this?

159
00:15:41,816 --> 00:15:44,694
Yes. And his aunt, Georgina Thomason.

160
00:15:44,861 --> 00:15:46,737
- Good, Bartlett.
- (Knock at door)

161
00:15:46,904 --> 00:15:48,698
Yes?

162
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,491
Sorry to interrupt you, sir.

163
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:53,369
- Thomason, lady to see you.
- Anything else?

164
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:56,038
No. You don't have to
dash off, do you?

165
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,374
No, absolutely not. George?

166
00:15:58,541 --> 00:16:01,377
Ken's got the fish food.
He'll be in later.

167
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:03,546
- Thanks.
- De nada.

168
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:06,382
- What do you think?
- We may be all right on the glass.

169
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:09,093
But what else are they
gonna come up with?

170
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:15,391
(Wolf whistle)

171
00:16:19,479 --> 00:16:23,858
Oh, George! Oh, my God,
I can't believe this is happening!

172
00:16:24,025 --> 00:16:26,611
That's not allowed in here, miss.

173
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,946
- Are you OK?
- It's all right.

174
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:31,491
I don't think I can handle this.

175
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:33,743
I was so afraid
to go to sleep last night, I...

176
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:36,412
Leave it out. Leave it out, OK?

177
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:39,999
Now listen, listen, listen, listen.
Listen.

178
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:44,128
You stayed at my place.

179
00:16:45,296 --> 00:16:48,925
We slept late. You made me breakfast.

180
00:16:53,763 --> 00:16:55,723
What?

181
00:16:55,890 --> 00:17:00,102
- What's he doing here?
- He wanted to see you.

182
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:03,105
Who did it, George? Kevin Delaney?

183
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:06,108
Want me to rub him out?
Anything. You name it.

184
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:10,279
- I have friends making enquiries.
- Good.

185
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:13,908
The jewels are very safe.

186
00:17:14,075 --> 00:17:17,620
If I get sent down, it all gets
handed back to cut my sentence.

187
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:22,250
Now, to cut my sentence even more,
I could tell them who done it with me,

188
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:25,962
if I wasn't very happy about everything.

189
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:29,465
What was the middle thing?

190
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:31,676
Piss off.

191
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:38,057
- You want me to spring you?
- Now!

192
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,981
George?

193
00:17:46,107 --> 00:17:49,068
- You don't think...?
- Do you?

194
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:51,153
No!

195
00:17:53,406 --> 00:17:55,324
No?

196
00:17:56,534 --> 00:17:58,995
- No.
- OK.

197
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:01,205
- George?
- What?

198
00:18:02,290 --> 00:18:04,792
Are you sure the garage is very safe?

199
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:08,462
Trust me.

200
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:11,048
Thank you very much.

201
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:13,718
Thanks a lot. Bye. Have a good day.

202
00:18:15,386 --> 00:18:18,180
- So?
- Well, he's not sure it was you.

203
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,515
What about you?

204
00:18:19,682 --> 00:18:22,602
He believes me.
He can't figure out you.

205
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:26,480
- Figure out what?
- If you turned him in or not, stupid!

206
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:31,027
Don't, uh, ever, ever,

207
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:34,322
ever call me stupid. OK?

208
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:38,868
What?

209
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:44,373
That's George's lawyer.

210
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,209
The other guy must be the barrister.

211
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:50,880
- So?
- Trust me.

212
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:56,469
- Let me know if anything turns up.
- Yes.

213
00:18:56,636 --> 00:18:58,721
Excuse me.

214
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:01,098
Don't I recognize you?

215
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:03,225
No. No, I don't think so.

216
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:04,894
Oh.

217
00:19:05,061 --> 00:19:08,105
But you are
a famous barrister, aren't you?

218
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:10,775
Er... well, hardly.

219
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:14,612
Well, could I have
your autograph anyway?

220
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:18,616
- Yes, yes. Certainly.
- Thanks.

221
00:19:19,492 --> 00:19:22,912
I'm studying aspects of your legal
system. I'm American.

222
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:25,581
- Oh, really?
- I've just started, though.

223
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:26,749
It's fascinating.

224
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:29,335
What, er, what brings you here?

225
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:33,506
Oh, it's a little embarrassing.
I... have a friend.

226
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:36,759
Oh! Oh, I see. Well, there you are.

227
00:19:36,926 --> 00:19:40,137
I knew it! You're Archie Leash!

228
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:42,264
- Leach.
- Right!

229
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:46,143
I saw you in court. Uh, two weeks ago.

230
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:49,605
- The casino break-in?
- You were great!

231
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:54,527
Oh, I'm a big fan of yours.
I love the way you... cross-examine.

232
00:19:56,487 --> 00:20:00,032
- Oh, I really admire your work.
- Thank you.

233
00:20:02,785 --> 00:20:05,955
- I'd better not...
- I don't suppose you...? No. Fine.

234
00:20:06,122 --> 00:20:07,498
Well...

235
00:20:08,082 --> 00:20:10,626
Thank you for this. I'll treasure it.

236
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:15,214
Au revoir.

237
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:19,427
You speak French, too.

238
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:22,805
(Wanda sighs)

239
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:40,990
What's going on?

240
00:20:41,157 --> 00:20:44,910
Whatever George decides to do,
he's gonna tell Leach first.

241
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:47,580
- Why?
- Because he's his lawyer.

242
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:51,834
- Yeah, yeah. I know that.
- So I'm gonna get to know Mr. Leach.

243
00:20:52,001 --> 00:20:54,462
George will tell him
where the diamonds are?

244
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:57,047
That's what I'm gonna find out.

245
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,228
You done well, my son.

246
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:13,898
Now, where are we going to hide it?

247
00:21:17,777 --> 00:21:23,365
Very good! Don't tell Wanda anything.
Otto might get something out of her.

248
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:25,868
- Now...
- George...

249
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:28,746
You are gonna g-g-get off, aren't you?

250
00:21:28,913 --> 00:21:33,167
Sure, don't worry about it, Ken.
We'll fix it. Now, anything on Otto?

251
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:36,212
Not yet.

252
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:38,088
You watch him.

253
00:21:41,217 --> 00:21:42,968
Ken?

254
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:45,805
OK.

255
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:48,557
Looks like the police
have been all over it.

256
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:52,228
Let me just change clothes,
and then I'll help you look.

257
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:56,607
(English accent)
Hello, K-K-Ken's p-p-pets.

258
00:21:57,358 --> 00:21:58,984
Hey!

259
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:02,905
Wake up! Wake up, limey fish!

260
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:08,410
So, how are you gonna
get friendly with this lawyer?

261
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:11,080
I don't know. I'll improvise.

262
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:12,748
Fucking insects!

263
00:22:12,915 --> 00:22:16,502
I thought Englishmen didn't like women,
the way they talk.

264
00:22:16,669 --> 00:22:21,423
No. He's straight. He's kinda cute,
too, in a pompous sort of way.

265
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:27,304
- You got the hots for him?
- I'm not into necrophilia.

266
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:29,098
(Otto laughs)

267
00:22:29,265 --> 00:22:31,934
What is this,
Hump a Limey Week suddenly?

268
00:22:32,101 --> 00:22:35,104
Otto doesn't approve.
Otto might get jealous.

269
00:22:35,855 --> 00:22:40,234
È molto pericoloso, signorina.

270
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:42,444
Molto pericolo...

271
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:51,787
- Carissima.
- Oh, speak it. Speak it!

272
00:22:52,538 --> 00:22:55,624
Un ossobuco milanese con piselli.

273
00:22:56,458 --> 00:23:01,589
Melanzane parmigiana con spinaci.

274
00:23:01,714 --> 00:23:04,800
- Dov'è la farmacia?
- Yes, yes, yes!

275
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:06,635
- No, no, no.
- Si, si, Si.

276
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:09,138
No, no, no. No, not here.

277
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:11,390
- Otto, no.
- Dov'è la Fontana di Trevi?

278
00:23:11,557 --> 00:23:14,059
- Not here, Otto!
- Um...

279
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:16,270
- Mozzarella.
- No! Not here.

280
00:23:16,437 --> 00:23:18,772
- Parmigiana. Gorgonzola!
- Otto, no!

281
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:20,107
Eh!

282
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:26,864
Wanda?

283
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:34,163
Look what I've got, Wanda.

284
00:23:35,706 --> 00:23:37,625
Treasure!

285
00:24:22,461 --> 00:24:24,380
- (Screams)
- Oh!

286
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:27,466
Oh, Ken, it's you!
I thought it was the police again.

287
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:30,386
Isn't it horrible about George? Oh, Ken!

288
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:33,722
I've such a headache.
Could you pick me up some aspirin?

289
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:35,265
(Clatter)

290
00:24:35,432 --> 00:24:38,477
- What's that?
- My brother. He's using the bathroom.

291
00:24:38,644 --> 00:24:41,105
- Otto?
- Mm. We just went and saw George.

292
00:24:41,271 --> 00:24:44,400
Oh, it was horrible, Ken.
It was just horrible.

293
00:24:48,904 --> 00:24:52,282
- Wh...
- Isn't it terrible about George?

294
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:55,411
When I find the bastard who squealed...!

295
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:57,746
I love that man!

296
00:24:57,913 --> 00:25:00,499
What are you d-d-doing here?

297
00:25:00,666 --> 00:25:02,751
What am I doing here?

298
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:05,004
Wanda was upset. She needed family.

299
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:09,717
Sh-sh-she just had a sh-sh-shower.

300
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:15,556
- I've got to speak to you.
- (Wanda wails)

